# Images are local-only by default (bucket map + retention:
# docs/conventions/workspace-hygiene.md). design-reference/ is re-included below.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
# macOS / iCloud Drive sync conflict-copies. The repo lives under an iCloud-synced
# ~/Documents path, so concurrent writes by parallel tools (Claude Code · Lovable ·
# Gemini · Antigravity) make iCloud spawn numbered duplicates like
# "feature-dashboard 2.md" or "src/components 2/". Never commit them — the canonical
# file is the unsuffixed one. Durable fix: move the repo off the iCloud-synced path.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]
* [0-9]/

# Local screenshots / visual artifacts (organized under docs/screenshots, kept local).
# Where each image goes + retention: docs/conventions/workspace-hygiene.md
docs/screenshots/

# Exception: canonical design-reference images ARE committed (file-placement
# policy — docs/README.md §"Where everything lives"). The global *.png/*.jpeg
# ignores above keep verification/QA captures local; these re-include only the
# curated references a parallel build (Lovable · Gemini · Antigravity · Claude
# Code) must match — one canonical image per screen, never a bulk dump.
!design-reference/**/*.png
!design-reference/**/*.jpeg
!design-reference/**/*.jpg
!design-reference/**/*.gif
!design-reference/**/*.webp

# Served social/preview image (the cosmic brand-band OG card) must be committed so it
# deploys and link previews work.
!public/og-cadence.png

# The film's poster frame (2026-08-12). Same reason as every exception in this
# block, and it was caught by the same failure this file already documents
# below: the global *.jpg rule silently swallowed it, `git add` refused it, and
# an unnoticed miss would have deployed the film with no poster - a black
# rectangle before anyone presses play, and no og:image on /film, which is the
# whole point of having a shareable URL for it.
#
# Scoped to the folder, not the filename, so a re-cut that renames the frame
# does not have to remember to come back here.
!public/film/*.jpg
# Served favicon / apple-touch marks (the app head references these) must be committed.
!public/favicon.png
!public/apple-touch-icon.png

# Brand kit (GTM): the ready-to-upload logo / icon / social raster set MUST be
# committed so we never rebuild the branding assets. Exception to the global
# *.png/*.jpg ignore, scoped to the branding folder only.
#
# PATH FIXED 2026-08-05. This pointed at "docs/Growth Strategy/branding/", a
# folder that was renamed to "docs/growth/" in the 2026-08-03 documentation
# cleanup. The exception was never moved with it, so for two days the rule above
# it silently won and every NEW brand raster was ignored. Files already in the
# index kept being tracked, which is why nothing looked broken: the old
# cadence-* PNGs and icons/ still showed up in git status while a freshly
# generated banner did not. The stale path is kept below so an old checkout
# still resolves.
!docs/growth/branding/**/*.png
!docs/growth/branding/**/*.jpg
!docs/Growth Strategy/branding/**/*.png
!docs/Growth Strategy/branding/**/*.jpg

# Claude Code runtime lock (machine-local state, never commit)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Large local-only v3 design reference exports (kept local, per founder 2026-07-05)
design-reference/Design reference for v3/
design-reference/Latest Design System - v3 /

# Nested working copies of this same repo (separate clones parked inside the
# checkout, 2026-07-24). They are stale checkouts of commits already on origin,
# so they carry no unique history, but they DO carry ~728 duplicate *.test.ts
# files that bun test discovers - which inflated the suite from ~379 files to
# 1137 and made the test gate unreadable. Never commit them; prefer deleting
# them outright once the founder confirms nothing local is wanted.
/supaprod/
/supaprod-v1/

# Temp screenshot dirs from verification sessions. One was committed by mistake.
.tmp-*/

# Local tool state (AgentDB, retired vector store). Loose at root until 2026-08-04.
.local/

# Lenny's Data paid archive, cloned to root 2026-08-10 (679 files, 61 MB).
# NEVER COMMIT. The paid licence forbids redistributing the raw files "in any
# form" - a private repo counts. It carries its own .git, so `git add -A` would
# record a broken submodule pointer rather than the files, but that protection
# is incidental and would vanish if the .git were ever removed.
# Other agents: do not re-upload it, clone your own from the pointer doc at
# docs/research/lennys-data-archive.md. Read the licence before quoting.
/lennys-newsletterpodcastdata-all/

# Cross-lane sprint coordination, created 2026-08-10 for the parallel design +
# engineering lanes. Untracked on purpose, for the same reason as
# .remember/remember.md: they are session-scoped scratch that both lanes read
# off disk in this checkout, not corpus documents. Keeping them untracked also
# keeps docs-doctor at WARN instead of the hard FAIL a stray tracked root file
# earns (scripts/docs-doctor.sh line 44), so neither lane's commits are blocked.
/HANDOFF-ENGINEERING.md
/DESIGN-LANE-STATUS.md
/POST-LAUNCH.md


# Lovable's plan-mode scratch. Calling `send_message` with plan_mode writes a
# plan file here, named with a date, and docs-doctor hard-FAILS on a dated
# filename. One was committed on 2026-08-10 (.lovable/plan/v3-v1-as-12-...md)
# and fails `bun run docs:check` for every lane on every run until it is
# untracked. Ignoring the directory stops the next one; the committed one still
# needs `git rm --cached`.
#
# Ignored rather than renamed because the plan is scratch for a single agent
# turn, not a document anybody reads later. `.lovable/project.json` and
# `.lovable/mcp/manifest.json` stay TRACKED - those are real project config.
/.lovable/plan/

# The one signed-in session every lane shares. Deliberately NOT under
# test-results/, which is playwright.config.ts outputDir and is DELETED at the
# start of every run (2026-08-11: one lane running any spec silently bricked
# browser verification for all the others).
playwright/.auth/
videos/supaprod-film/renders/video-4k.mp4
videos/supaprod-film/renders/supaprod-film-final-4k.mp4

# Film reference frames and scroll captures. The global *.png/*.jpg rules above
# swallowed these, which meant 25 reference images existed only on one laptop.
# They are 14 MB total and they are the visual record behind every render in
# videos/supaprod-film/renders/, which IS tracked. Founder ruling 2026-08-13:
# nothing but secrets lives only on local.
!videos/supaprod-film/snapshots/**/*.png
!videos/supaprod-film/snapshots/**/*.jpg
!videos/supaprod-film/capture/screenshots/**/*.png
docs/pitch/applications/sweep/.msg

# Large media staged in shareables for upload. Masters live in videos/ and stay out of git.
docs/pitch/shareables/*.mp4
docs/pitch/shareables/*.mov

# Skill-installer symlinks into .agents/, same pattern as the batch above.
.claude/skills/brag
.kiro/skills/brag

# vercel/ai's use-ai-sdk skill, installed 2026-08-23. skills-lock.json pins it by hash
# (2d6ed9b89) so a fresh checkout reinstalls the identical file; the materialised SKILL.md
# is an install artifact. Ignored because a permanently untracked path is not free here:
# both lanes are told to read `git status --porcelain` in a quiet worktree to spot a request
# written and never pushed, and every standing `??` line makes that signal harder to read.
.claude/skills/ai-sdk
.kiro/skills/ai-sdk

# Python bytecode. scripts/ carries funding-sync.py, rank-funding-programmes.py and
# check-application-sources.py; importing any of them writes a __pycache__ that was
# showing up as untracked and would eventually be committed by a wide git add.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

